WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:08.551
Long, long ago two boys were born on the same day in the same city.

2
00:00:08.552 --> 00:00:14.643
Tom Canty was born to a poor family, who couldn't afford another child.

3
00:00:14.644 --> 00:00:23.684
Prince Edward was born to a royal family, who welcomed the new heir to the throne.

4
00:00:23.685 --> 00:00:29.437
A dozen years later, both boys lived by the river.

5
00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:38.435
While Edward lived in a magnificent palace, Tom lived in a shabby room in a poor neighborhood.

6
00:00:38.436 --> 00:00:46.146
While Edward's father was King Henry, Tom's father was John Canty, a thief.

7
00:00:46.147 --> 00:00:55.673
John often made Tom and his sister, Nancy, beg for money.

8
00:00:55.674 --> 00:01:02.897
As Tom headed out to beg one January morning, he met Father Andrew.

9
00:01:02.898 --> 00:01:08.235
The priest had taught him how to read and write as well as some Latin.

10
00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:16.059
But what Tom liked best were Father Andrew's tales of palaces and princes.

11
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.494
"Do you have a story for me today, Father?" Tom asked.

12
00:01:20.495 --> 00:01:24.988
"Of course!" the priest said as they walked together.

13
00:01:24.989 --> 00:01:29.300
"Once upon a time there was a prince named Richard . . ."

14
00:01:29.301 --> 00:01:35.947
Because of Father Andrew's wonderful stories, Tom sometimes pretended to be a prince.

15
00:01:35.948 --> 00:01:44.264
This amused his friends, but they also enjoyed his game—except when he made them the servants.

16
00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:50.696
All too soon Tom and Father Andrew arrived at the priest's church.

17
00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:55.538
"We'll finish Prince Richard's story later," Father Andrew said.

18
00:01:55.539 --> 00:02:01.468
"I can't wait!" Then Tom sighed.

19
00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:08.634
"It's time to ask strangers for money."

20
00:02:08.635 --> 00:02:13.429
Tom hated begging, but his family needed the money.

21
00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:20.501
Most people ignored him, so he was surprised when someone tapped his shoulder later that day.

22
00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:26.523
"What's this? A prince begging?"

23
00:02:26.524 --> 00:02:31.757
Tom turned to find his best friend, Julian Witt, laughing.

24
00:02:31.758 --> 00:02:37.855
"You have mocked royalty and are sentenced to prison!" Tom joked.

25
00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:42.165
Then, in his regular voice, he added, "I need a break.

26
00:02:42.166 --> 00:02:46.294
Let's see if anybody wants to play by the river."

27
00:02:46.295 --> 00:02:51.602
Julian turned pale. "The river?"

28
00:02:51.603 --> 00:02:55.518
"Oh, sorry! I forgot about what happened to you there.

29
00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:59.666
We'll stay away from the water today."

30
00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:04.977
The boys found their friends, and the afternoon passed quickly.

31
00:03:04.978 --> 00:03:12.561
Prince Tom pardoned Julian, gave orders to his army, and met with his royal advisers.

32
00:03:12.562 --> 00:03:18.462
"Your Highness, the sun is setting," Julian said.

33
00:03:18.463 --> 00:03:26.333
"Oh no!" Tom gulped. "I have only one coin for my father!"

34
00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:33.655
For a moment Tom thought about not going home, but he didn't want to miss supper.

35
00:03:33.656 --> 00:03:41.854
Reluctantly, he said good-bye and headed home.

36
00:03:41.855 --> 00:03:49.247
"Where have you been?" Tom's father yelled. "You'd better have lots of money!"

37
00:03:49.248 --> 00:03:57.173
"People weren't in a generous mood." Tom handed over his one coin.

38
00:03:57.174 --> 00:04:02.571
"'A generous mood.'" John Canty echoed Tom's words.

39
00:04:02.572 --> 00:04:08.383
"Where do you learn this stuff? Probably from that priest."

40
00:04:08.384 --> 00:04:11.151
That reminded Tom of something.

41
00:04:11.152 --> 00:04:18.322
"I wonder if Father Andrew has any books about Prince Richard," he thought. "Maybe I could—"

42
00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:25.638
"Are you listening?" John shouted. "I said, go to bed!"

43
00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:31.337
"Oh, don't send him to bed without supper," Tom's mother pleaded.

44
00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:36.201
Meanwhile Nancy tried to stay out of her father's way.

45
00:04:36.202 --> 00:04:43.980
"Don't interfere!" John said to his wife. "To bed, Tom! Now!"

46
00:04:43.981 --> 00:04:49.033
Tom went to a corner and untangled some old blankets.

47
00:04:49.034 --> 00:04:54.986
He made himself as comfortable as possible on the straw covering the wood floor.

48
00:04:54.987 --> 00:05:01.966
But for a long time, his hunger and his parents' arguing kept him awake.

49
00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:06.054
He tried to distract himself.

50
00:05:06.055 --> 00:05:11.986
"How many princes has Father Andrew told me about?" Tom thought.

51
00:05:11.987 --> 00:05:17.147
"William, Richard, James . . ."

52
00:05:17.148 --> 00:05:21.637
Tom drifted off, thinking of a distant kingdom.

53
00:05:21.638 --> 00:05:29.775
In his dream he was surrounded by lords and ladies, beautiful music, and delicious food.

54
00:05:29.776 --> 00:05:37.176
Everyone bowed to Prince Tom and obeyed his orders.

55
00:05:37.177 --> 00:05:43.926
The next morning Tom awoke in the same filthy room on Offal Street.

56
00:05:43.927 --> 00:05:49.867
He was still hungry and still wearing his ragged clothes.

57
00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:54.041
Tom sighed with disappointment.

58
00:05:54.042 --> 00:06:01.390
"I'll only be a prince in my dreams," he thought, slipping outside before anyone else woke up.

59
00:06:01.391 --> 00:06:07.490
"But maybe someday I'll meet a real one."

60
00:06:07.491 --> 00:06:13.475
As Tom wandered along the river, he lost track of time and where he was.

61
00:06:13.476 --> 00:06:18.745
After a while he came upon a magnificent building.

62
00:06:18.746 --> 00:06:24.492
Tom's eyes grew wide. "Could this be the king's palace?"

63
00:06:24.493 --> 00:06:29.015
He joined a few people waiting near a golden gate.

64
00:06:29.016 --> 00:06:35.079
Suddenly a boy and a man appeared in the courtyard beyond the gate.

65
00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:40.711
Dressed in silk and velvet, the boy wore a sword at his hip.

66
00:06:40.712 --> 00:06:44.508
Tom heard the man call the boy "Your Highness."

67
00:06:44.509 --> 00:06:49.396
"A prince!" Tom rushed forward for a better look.

68
00:06:49.397 --> 00:06:55.313
Immediately a guard grabbed Tom's hand and jerked him away.

69
00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:58.354
"Step back, you pauper!"

70
00:06:58.355 --> 00:07:04.052
The people laughed.

71
00:07:04.053 --> 00:07:08.076
But the prince ran to the gate and scolded the guard.

72
00:07:08.077 --> 00:07:11.376
"How dare you treat a poor boy like that!

73
00:07:11.377 --> 00:07:21.629
Open the gate at once, and let him in!"

